   "id": "muster",
   "title": "The Franks gather at La Saphorie",
   "time": "Late June - 2 July 1187",
   "narrative": "Saladin crossed the Jordan on 30 June with the largest army he had ever led, about 40,000 men of whom some 12,000 were regular cavalry, and camped at Kafr Sabt. The Frankish host, 18,000 to 20,000 strong with some 1,200 knights, waited at the well-watered castle of La Saphorie, a strong position with water close at hand. On 2 July Saladin stormed Tiberias, the town of Count Raymond, in the hope that its fall would draw the Franks out of their camp. Raymond's wife held on in the citadel.",
