  {
   "id": "council",
   "title": "The night council",
   "time": "Night of 2 July",
   "narrative": "That night Raymond of Tripoli argued that a march across the dry hills to Tiberias was exactly what Saladin wanted, and that the camp at La Saphorie should be held while Tiberias, his own town, was given up if need be. Gerard de Ridefort and Raynald of Chatillon answered by calling him a coward. King Guy sided with them and ordered the army out at once against Saladin.",
