  },
  {
   "id": "march",
   "title": "The march into the heat",
   "time": "Morning, 3 July",
   "narrative": "The Frankish army left La Saphorie and struggled east in the July heat, with Raymond's division in front and Balian's and Joscelin's men in the rear. Muslim mounted archers harassed it from the first mile. The Springs of Turan gave far too little water for such a host. Saladin, learning the Franks had left their water, broke off from Tiberias and brought his army out to meet them.",
