  {
   "id": "turn",
   "title": "Veering for Hattin",
   "time": "Midday, 3 July",
   "narrative": "At midday Raymond judged that the army could not reach Tiberias by nightfall, and he and Guy turned it left toward the springs at Kafr Hattin, about nine kilometres off, to drink there and go down to the lake next day. Saladin's men slid between the Franks and the water, and the column, hemmed in and tormented by thirst, had to halt on the dry plateau near Meskenah. Reaching the wells that day had become impossible.",
