  {
   "id": "night",
   "title": "A night without water",
   "time": "Night of 3-4 July",
   "narrative": "The Franks pitched camp on the arid plateau, so closely ringed that, in one chronicler's phrase, a cat could not have slipped out. The Muslims prayed, sang and beat drums through the dark, and set fire to the dry grass so that smoke and heat added to the thirst. Their own camels brought skins of water up from the lake. Fresh arrows, 400 camel loads of them, reached Gokbori's archers.",
