   "title": "Smoke and arrows",
   "time": "Dawn, 4 July",
   "narrative": "Morning showed the Franks blinded by smoke from the grass fires and under steady fire from Gokbori's horse archers on the left of Saladin's line. Gerard and Raynald urged Guy to form for battle and fight through. Raymond took the first division with Raymond of Antioch, Guy the centre with the True Cross, while Balian and Joscelin of Edessa brought up the rear.",
