  {
   "id": "advance",
   "title": "Raymond's charge",
   "time": "Morning, 4 July",
   "narrative": "Thirsty and sapped, the Franks broke camp and headed again for the springs of Hattin, but Saladin's army blocked the road ahead and fell on the ragged column from behind as well. Count Raymond led two charges to break through to the lake and its water. The Muslim ranks parted before the second charge and let him through, and he reached the shore and rode on to Tyre.",
