   "title": "Guy and Raynald before Saladin",
   "time": "Evening, 4 July",
   "narrative": "Guy, his brother Amalric, Raynald of Chatillon, Gerard de Ridefort and many other barons were taken. Guy and Raynald were brought to Saladin's tent. Saladin offered Guy a cup of water, which among Muslims meant mercy, and Guy passed it on to Raynald; Saladin knocked it away, saying he had not offered it to that evil man, and accused Raynald of breaking the truce. Raynald was killed, by Saladin's own sword in some reports. Guy was told that kings do not kill kings.",
